><p><b>Give a phone number in pairs, using your own or an invented one.</b></p><p style=\"opacity:.7;\">For example: “Mon numéro est le zéro six, douze, trente-quatre, cinquante-six.”</p></div>","recordPrompt":"Now it's your turn to speak!","expectedText":"Mon numéro est le zéro six, douze, trente-quatre, cinquante-six.","size":null,"created":{"_seconds":1793275903,"_nanoseconds":45000000}},{"id":"wpKHxqlAxqP7k6p1qTCc","level":"a0-tout-public","lesson":20,"part":14,"type":"text","name":"ab-adults-l20-p14-b1","partTitle":"Well done","transitionMode":"button","url":null,"imageUrl":null,"content":"<div style=\"text-align:center;\"><div style=\"font-size:64px;line-height:1.1;\">📞</div><p><b>Contact details ready!</b></p></div><p style=\"line-height:1.6;\">🧑‍🏫 You can give your address and a phone number, in French pairs. That is a very useful survival skill.</p>","recordPrompt":null,"expectedText":null,"size":null,"created":{"_seconds":1793275902,"_nanoseconds":981000000}}]